{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509591-aftermath-of-destroying-the-five-talons-of-the-wyrm","id":1509591,"title":"Aftermath of destroying the five Talons of the Wyrm?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-25T09:10:45-07:00","id":1509591,"title":"Aftermath of destroying the five Talons of the Wyrm?","content":"We all know that destroying a Maeljin Incarna has a major effect on the rest of the world. What would destroying a Wyrm Talon, or even all of them, be likely to accomplish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-25-2023, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T10:53:27-07:00","id":1509598,"title":"","content":"According to Garou myth, the Talons of the Wyrm are the result of the first direct attack on Gaia. He manifested a gigantic hand that corrupted everything it touched, until brave Garou warriors managed to rip the hand into shreds. And while the Wyrm was forced to retreat, his fingers had clawed themselves deep into Gaia and managed to flee the Garou by changing their form. They were primal manifestations of the Wyrm, the physical stuff of its first manifestation in the world of matter, and were thus almost indestructible by any force. But the Garou were able, through great feats and earth magic, to bind them into objects. Garou mystics speculate about the exact number of talons, but a few are known and rightly feared by the Garou Nation, for should all Talons be freed from their ancient prisons, the Apocalypse would surely begin.<br /> There are no stats, official or otherwise, detailing the exact nature of the Talons in their &quot;pure&quot;/unimprisoned forms. It's unknown if there were four or five Talons (even the Garou have forgotten exactly how many Talons there were.<br /> <br /> <b>Narlthus</b>, the Thumb \u2013 banished into a star stone in the Far North, prison is currently held by Black Spiral Dancers who try to free him. - WTA: Rite of Passage<br /> <b>Koshchei</b>, the First Finger &quot;He-Who-Points&quot; \u2013 banished into the Soul egg by the Silver Fangs and held by Uktena Banetenders later freed by Baba Yaga, current status unknown.- WTA: Rage Across Russia<br /> <b>Thrassus, &quot;</b>the Thrice Damned&quot;, the Smallest Finger, sealed beneath the Sept of Bygone Visions in the Mediterranean, a caern under control of the Black Furies. It has been lost/stolen from the Sept. It is imprisoned inside a three foot long cylinder made of an apparently unscratchable form of glass (if the transparent material is indeed glass) containing a thick blue-green fluid of unknown substance. The cylinder is labeled as &quot;Exhibit 338&quot; (but was nicknamed the &quot;Anti-Christ Serum&quot; by a security guard who had seen too many John Carpenter films) inside a secure government storage facility, location unknown. - WTA: Book of the Weaver<br /> (<i>Book of the Weaver</i> and <i>Rage Across Russia</i> both hint that there is a forgotten Talon of the Wyrm also imprisoned inside one of the many artifacts and fetishes the Black Furies are storing inside the Womb at the Sept of Bygone Visions in Ecube, Greece. (The Sept itself is described in <i>Caerns: Places of Power</i>) it is highly possible it was <b>Thrassus</b>\u200b<br /> <b>Heartsplinter</b> - WTA: The Last Battle (this is a bit wonky, since this from the Time of Judgment novel <i>The Last Battle</i> by Bill Bridges; It escaped from its prison (the nature of which isn't revealed) and slew its Uktena Banetenders. It manifested as a green mist in the Umbra, but dwelled in the hearts of Garou within several miles of its location, forcing them to frenzy constantly)<br /> <b><i>Something</i> </b>is lying buried somewhere in the Arctic Circle, hidden underneath a half-froznen slit, guarded by aquatic monsters and banes; the Wendigo <i>belives</i> it is a Talon of the Wyrm - The Blood-Dimmed Tide\u200b\u200b<br /> <b><i>Something</i> </b>\u200bis imprisoned at the Black Fury caern, the Sept of Artemis, it is suggested, it is a Talon of the Wyrm - WTA: Werewolf Players Guide (1993)<br /> <b><i>Something</i> </b>\u200bis in the Black Fury caern Sept of the Black Pegasus, it is suggested, it is a Talon of the Wyrm - WTA: Werewolf Players Guide (1993)\u200b<br /> <br /> What would destroying a Wyrm Talon, or even all of them, be likely to accomplish?<br /> Probably nothing<br /> This is my personal oppinion, but they are not like the Maeljin. The Maeljin are actually not part of the Wyrm, yet have tremendous effect on the world <i>exactly becasue of that; they were part of it</i> before ascended in to Maeljin status.<b>Empress Aliara </b>is rumored to have been a popular courtesan during Caliph Haroun al-Raschid\u2019s reign. <b>Lady Aife </b>was once an enthusiastic torturer for the Spanish Inquisition. The current <b>Lord Steel </b>was once a conquistador who sacked the native civilizations of Central and South America. <b>Hellbringer </b>was a Viking berserker. <b>Thurifuge</b> was a surgeon and war criminal from the Nazi death camps <br /> And so on<br /> But the Tallons never were the part of the world, and while they are around Antediluvian level powerhouses [Baba Yaga summoned Koshchei AND the Zmei and even they were not enough to destroy Absimiliard, and while he was &quot;young&quot; back then; Baba Yaga was Embraced around 5000 BC, and Absimilliard was embraced 3000 years before that (- or more, of course if we accept Vasilisa was twice the age of Baba Yaga...) - Anyhow, even a Tallon of the Wyrm AND the Zmei was not enough to off Absimilliard] they are not really... had a real effect on the world.<br /> As far as we know it, but correct me if I'm wrong<br /> <br /> The Talons of the Wyrm are &quot;part&quot; of the Wyrm, broken of and became seperate entites, like the Urge Wyrms; I think if somehow the would be destroyed, they would just return to their source, the Wyrm - <i>or their loss would actually weaken </i>the already wounded and trapped in the Weaver's Web Wyrm to the point it could be possibly destroyed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T13:21:15-07:00","id":1509626,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> how do you gather all these tidbits so efficiently when you give answers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T15:45:09-07:00","id":1509633,"title":"","content":"Absolutely amazing response. If I were ever to play it I might want to make it so there was some payoff, like with the Heartsplinter and frenzy, but your response is well thought out, and probably the most logical anyone could have given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T22:00:08-07:00","id":1509688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509591-aftermath-of-destroying-the-five-talons-of-the-wyrm?p=1509626#post1509626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> how do you gather all these tidbits so efficiently when you give answers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am standing on the shoulders of giants <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> And have a solid three decade of WoD under my belt, mostly spent as a Storyteller, have basically all the supplements, familiar with the game lines and absolutelly love crossover games; done my fair share of research, because while the Golden Rule (aka. it is Your Game, do whatever you like and enjoy) is always an option I like to stay in the &quot;canon&quot; and belivable territory (and no, Okullos killing from Obfuscate Rayzeel, a 4th Gen Salubri with Auspex AND Fortitude and in Golconda with a flaregun is NOT that, just for the record <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and have a few tonns of notes and theories and like to spend my time making new ones supported by the (everchanging) cannon lore<br /> Well at least I try<br /> And most of the questions were already asked in some form or in other, the rest is just dusting off the memory and digging up the answers lying around somewhere<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509591-aftermath-of-destroying-the-five-talons-of-the-wyrm?p=1509633#post1509633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely amazing response.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprow